  "problem": "$(3+7\\,\\text{i})(3+3\\,\\text{i})=$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying two complex numbers is similar to multiplying two binomials. We also use the fact that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+7\\,\\text{i})(3+3\\,\\text{i}) & =3\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 3\\,\\text{i}+7\\,\\text{i}\\cdot 3+7\\,\\text{i}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =9+9\\,\\text{i}+21\\,\\text{i}+21\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =9+30\\,\\text{i}+21\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =9+30\\,\\text{i}-21 \\\\  & =-12+30\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
